{"name":"Silver Bird","hex":"#fbf5f0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silver","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lustrous, white, metallic element, atomic number 47, atomic weight 107.87, symbol Ag.","Coins made from silver or any similar white metal."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made from silver.","Made from another white metal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silver"},{"term":"bird","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An animal of the clade (traditionally class) Aves in the phylum Chordata, characterized by being warm-blooded, having feathers and wings usually capable of flight, having a beaked mouth, and laying eggs.","Any winged animal."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To observe or identify wild birds in their natural environment.","To catch or shoot birds; to hunt birds."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bird"}],"entries":[{"title":"IRS Airlines","blocks":[{"text":"IRS Airlines Limited was an airline based in Abuja, Nigeria. It operated scheduled domestic passenger services. Its main base was Nnamdi Azikiwe International Airport. The airline was established in 2002 and started operations in March 2002. It ceased operations in 2013. The company slogan was Now you can go places."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0e/IRS_Airlines_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IRS_Airlines"},{"title":"Silverbird Group","blocks":[{"text":"The Silverbird Group is a diversified multi-media company with holdings in Radio, Television, Real Estate, and Cinemas headquartered in Lagos, Nigeria. The company was established in 1980 by Ben Murray-Bruce and counts Silverbird Cinemas and the Most Beautiful Girl in Nigeria (MBGN) and Mr Nigeria pageants amongst its holdings. Its businesses divisions are Silverbird Properties, Silverbird Film Distribution, Silverbird Communications, Silverbird Cinemas, Silverbird Production, and Dream Magic Studios."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/94/Silverbird_Group_logo.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silverbird_Group"},{"title":"Silver Bird (streamliner)","blocks":[{"text":"Silver Bird was a motorcycle land-speed record setting streamliner motorcycle. It was powered by two motors delivering 240 horsepower (180 kW). It was the first motorcycle to set a speed record over 300 miles per hour (480 km/h), when ridden by Don Vesco at the Bonneville Speedway in 1975."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/A_PB_Vesco-Kawasaki05.jpg/330px-A_PB_Vesco-Kawasaki05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_Bird_(streamliner)"},{"title":"Silver Bird (Mark Lindsay song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Silver Bird\" is a song written by Kenny Young and recorded by Mark Lindsay, in his solo career after Paul Revere and the Raiders."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/48/Silver_Bird_-_Mark_Lindsay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_Bird_(Mark_Lindsay_song)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Fokker_100_IRS_Airlines_5N-HIR_Ikeja_April_2009.jpg/500px-Fokker_100_IRS_Airlines_5N-HIR_Ikeja_April_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Fokker_100_IRS_Airlines_5N-HIR_Ikeja_April_2009.jpg/500px-Fokker_100_IRS_Airlines_5N-HIR_Ikeja_April_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Fokker F100 belonging to the airline at Murtala Muhammed International Airport","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFokker_100_IRS_Airlines_5N-HIR_Ikeja_April_2009.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Silverbird_cinema_building%2C_Lagos.jpeg/500px-Silverbird_cinema_building%2C_Lagos.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Silverbird_cinema_building%2C_Lagos.jpeg/1280px-Silverbird_cinema_building%2C_Lagos.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Silverbird_cinema_building%2C_Lagos.jpeg/500px-Silverbird_cinema_building%2C_Lagos.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Silverbird cinema building, Victoria Island, Lagos","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASilverbird_cinema_building%2C_Lagos.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Silver_Bird_streamliner_1974.jpg/500px-Silver_Bird_streamliner_1974.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Silver_Bird_streamliner_1974.jpg/1280px-Silver_Bird_streamliner_1974.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Silver_Bird_streamliner_1974.jpg/500px-Silver_Bird_streamliner_1974.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Silver Bird c. 1974 with shorter stabilizing fin than on the 1975 record setting run","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASilver_Bird_streamliner_1974.jpg"}],"sounds":{"silver":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b9/En-us-silver.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b9/En-us-silver.ogg/En-us-silver.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src"